```jsx
import React, { useEffect, useRef, useState } from 'react';
import cytoscape from 'cytoscape';
import { connect, useSelector, useDispatch } from 'react-redux';
import { fetchData } from '../actions/graphActions';
import cxtmenu from 'cytoscape-cxtmenu';
import dagre from 'cytoscape-dagre';

cytoscape.use(cxtmenu);
cytoscape.use(dagre);

const VisNetwork = ({ data, loading, error }) => {
  const ref = useRef(null);
  const dispatch = useDispatch();

  useEffect(() => {
    dispatch(fetchData());
  }, [dispatch]);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (data && data.nodes && data.edges) {
      const cy = cytoscape({
        container: ref.current,
        elements: { nodes: data.nodes, edges: data.edges },
        style: [
          {
            selector: 'node',
            style: {
              'background-color': '#666',
              'label': 'data(id)',
              'text-valign': 'top',
              'text-halign': 'center',
              'height': 10,
              'width': 10,
              'border-width': 1,
              'line-color': '#ccc',
              'target-arrow-color': '#ccc',
              'target-arrow-shape': 'triangle',
            },
          },
          {
            selector: 'edge',
            style: {
              'target-arrow-color': '#ccc',
              'target-arrow-shape': 'triangle',
            },
          },
        ],
        layout: { name: 'dagre' },
      });
    }
  }, [data]);

  if (loading) return <div>Loading...</div>;
  if (error) return <div>Error: {error}</div>;

  return <div ref={ref}></div>;
};

const mapStateToProps = (state) => ({
  data: state.graph.data,
  loading: state.graph.loading,
  error: state.graph.error,
});

export default connect(mapStateToProps)(VisNetwork);
```

This code creates a `VisNetwork` component that uses Cytoscape to render a graph. It connects to Redux to fetch the graph data and uses the `fetchData` action to retrieve the data. The component also handles loading and error states.

The `useEffect` hook dispatches the `fetchData` action when the component mounts. Another `useEffect` hook updates the Cytoscape instance when the `data` prop changes.

The `mapStateToProps` function maps the Redux state to the component's props, providing access to the graph data, loading, and error states.

Finally, the `connect` function from `react-redux` connects the `VisNetwork` component to the Redux store.
