<first_data>
The Steam Controller is a game controller developed by Valve Corporation for use with games on their digital distribution platform, Steam. It was designed to provide a versatile and customizable gaming experience for PC games that were traditionally played with a keyboard and mouse. The controller features a unique layout with dual trackpads that can mimic the precision of a mouse, as well as a touch screen for navigating menus and in-game interfaces.

The left trackpad is typically used for movement, similar to an analog stick on other controllers, while the right trackpad can be used for looking around or aiming. The touch screen can be used for a variety of functions, such as displaying a virtual keyboard or acting as additional buttons. The controller also includes haptic feedback motors in each trackpad to provide tactile feedback for various actions in games.

The Steam Controller was released in November 2015 and has received mixed reviews from gamers due to its unconventional design and learning curve. However, it has also been praised for its versatility and customization options, allowing users to create custom control schemes for any game on Steam. In May 2019, Valve announced that they would no longer produce the Steam Controller, but existing units can still be used and supported by Steam.
