`return (sizeof(fsa_t) + (block\_size \* num\_of\_blocks) + sizeof(size\_t));`

You have forgotten to align the block size before multiplying it by the number of blocks. The correct line would be:

`return (sizeof(fsa_t) + (ALIGN(block\_size) \* num\_of\_blocks) + sizeof(size\_t));`

This bug would result in incorrect pool size calculation and could lead to buffer overflows or other undefined behavior.
