<first_data>
To achieve this functionality in WooCommerce, you can use a custom function that checks if Cyprus is selected as the country in the checkout form. If it is, then the city and postcode fields will be hidden and marked as not required.

Here's an example of how you could implement this using a custom plugin or by adding the code to your theme's functions.php file:

1. First, create a custom plugin or add the following code to your theme's functions.php file:
```php
add_action( 'wp_enqueue_scripts', 'custom_checkout_fields_css' );
add_action( 'woocommerce_before_checkout_form', 'custom_hide_checkout_fields', 10 );
add_filter( 'woocommerce_checkout_get_value', 'custom_unset_checkout_field_values', 10, 2 );
```
1. Then, add the following functions to your custom plugin or functions.php file:
```php
function custom_checkout_fields_css() {
    $css = "
        .hide-for-cyprus {
            display: none !important;
        }
    ";
    wp_add_inline_style( 'woocommerce-layout', $css );
}

function custom_hide_checkout_fields() {
    global $woocommerce;

    if ( isset( $_POST['country'] ) && 'CY' === strtoupper( $_POST['country'] ) ) {
        echo '<script>jQuery(".checkout.billing_country-field + .form-row .form-row-wide").addClass("hide-for-cyprus");</script>';
    }
}

function custom_unset_checkout_field_values( $value, $key ) {
    if ( 'billing_city' === $key || 'billing_postcode' === $key ) {
        $country = WC()->checkout->get_value( 'billing_country' );

        if ( 'CY' === strtoupper( $country ) ) {
            return '';
        }
    }

    return $value;
}
```
1. Finally, add the following JavaScript code to your custom plugin or functions.php file or enqueue it as a separate script:
```php
add_action( 'wp_footer', 'custom_hide_checkout_fields_js' );

function custom_hide_checkout_fields_js() {
    ?>
    <script>
        jQuery(document).ready(function($) {
            var countrySelect = $('#billing_country');
            var cityField = $('.checkout.billing_city-field');
            var postcodeField = $('.checkout.billing_postcode-field');

            if ('CY' === countrySelect.val()) {
                cityField.closest('.form-row').addClass('hide-for-cyprus');
                postcodeField.closest('.form-row').addClass('hide-for-cyprus');
            }

            countrySelect.change(function() {
                if ('CY' === $(this).val()) {
                    cityField.closest('.form-row').addClass('hide-for-cyprus');
                    postcodeField.closest('.form-row').addClass('hide-for-cyprus');
                } else {
                    cityField.closest('.form-row').removeClass('hide-for-cyprus');
                    postcodeField.closest('.form-row').removeClass('hide-for-cyprus');
                }
            });
        });
    </script>
    <?php
}
```
This code will hide the city and postcode fields and mark them as not required when Cyprus is selected as the country during checkout. Note that hiding these fields may cause issues with the validation of the checkout form. To fully remove the requirement for these fields, you would need to modify the WooCommerce core files, which is not recommended. Instead, consider using a plugin like WooCommerce Checkout Manager or Advanced Custom Fields for WooCommerce to customize the checkout fields more easily and safely.
